Verc uses libVLC's public C API and VLC's filter interfaces. The
standalone build includes selected VLC 3.x libraries and playback plugins.
VLC and libVLC retain their own licenses and copyrights. Build-only plugin
headers are from VLC 3.0.24; their LGPL license is in Vendor/VLC/COPYING.LIB.

The build downloads VLC 3.0.24. It does not fetch the corresponding source code.
Before you distribute that build, provide the complete corresponding source and
license notices for that exact VLC build and its dependencies, as their licenses
require. Check the licenses of the copied plugins. Some VLC configurations
contain GPL v3 components and are not suitable for a GPL v2-only distribution.

VLC source: https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc
VLC releases: https://download.videolan.org/pub/videolan/vlc/
libVLC documentation: https://videolan.videolan.me/vlc-3.0/

Verc uses Apple system frameworks and SF Symbols from macOS. Verc does not
include separate SF Symbols font files. Apple terms apply to those resources.

The animated drop icon adapts Material Line Icons by Vjacheslav Trushkin
to native SwiftUI. Its MIT license is in LineMD-LICENSE.txt.
Source: https://github.com/cyberalien/line-md

The start page adapts vgpu's prism scene to Metal, including its beveled mesh,
spectral light mesh, optical equations, studio reflections, bloom, and dust.
Copyright (c) 2025 Vercel, Inc. Its MIT license is in Vgpu-LICENSE.txt.
Source: https://github.com/vercel-labs/vgpu/tree/9c23f6c02db06cff4a4c4d38656c0e6f1bda203f/apps/docs/app/%5Blang%5D/%28home%29/components/prism-background

VLC provides the playback reference. Vercel provides the visual reference.
